  "segments": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 7.94,
      "duration": 7.94,
      "text": "In the last topic, we established what an AI agent is, a system that doesn't just respond, but acts."
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "start": 8.34,
      "end": 17.76,
      "duration": 9.42,
      "text": "We introduced Solara Energy and looked at how agents can take a goal like monitoring site performance and turn it into a sequence of real actions,"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "start": 18.38,
      "end": 23.32,
      "duration": 4.94,
      "text": "querying data, comparing outputs, flagging anomalies, and generating reports."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "start": 23.82,
      "end": 26.54,
      "duration": 2.72,
      "text": "But not all agents work the same way."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "start": 26.54,
      "end": 34.1,
      "duration": 7.56,
      "text": "There are different types built on different architectures designed for different kinds of problems."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "start": 36.14,
      "end": 42.32,
      "duration": 6.18,
      "text": "And understanding those differences is what allows you to match the right agent to the right job."
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "start": 42.88,
      "end": 48.58,
      "duration": 5.7,
      "text": "By the end of this topic, you will be able to describe the core components that make up an AI"
    }
  ],
